{
  "rationale": "The plant models perception and motion as a single automaton, capturing all possible sensor outcomes and motion commands. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is preferred in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and recovery turns are chosen conservatively after obstacles. Full_rotate is reserved for repeated or dead-end obstacles. All obstacle events force a turn recovery before returning to exploration. The design avoids oscillations and infinite controllable loops, and ensures all uncontrollables are handled in every state.",
  "strategy": [
    "Single plant automaton for combined perception and motion, with all uncontrollable and controllable events.",
    "Specification automaton encodes safe, coverage-biased exploration: random_walk in clear, move_forward for progress, rotate recovery after obstacles, and full_rotate only as last resort."
